From ca3da88cd8d01f6e6da3b2c38743859114f79355 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Montleon <jmontleo@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:23:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] compat(macos): run the control CLI on macOS as well as Linux

The rhwa-lab CLI runs locally on the operator's machine (it SSHes to a Linux
EC2 host for everything else). A few locally-run commands were GNU/Linux-only;
make them portable so the tool works on macOS (Intel + Apple Silicon) too.
Code that runs over SSH on the Linux host is unchanged.

- openshift.sh: the LOCAL oc was always the Linux client tarball, which won't
  execute on macOS. Select the client for the local OS/arch via uname
  (mac / mac-arm64 / linux). os_host_tools still fetches the Linux client --
  that one runs on the Linux EC2 host.
- odf.sh: `base64 -w0` is GNU-only (macOS/BSD base64 has no -w); use
  `base64 | tr -d '\n'`, which yields one unwrapped line on both. Replace bare
  `mktemp` (BSD mktemp requires a template) with an explicit template.
- tests: portable `mktemp` templates; drop bash-4-only `declare -A` from two
  stubs (macOS ships bash 3.2) in favor of a file-backed / case-based stub; add
  client_arch_test.sh covering the OS/arch client selection.
- README: note Linux/macOS support (no GNU coreutils needed; stock bash 3.2 ok)
  and that only the local CLI is cross-platform.

Product bash is otherwise 3.2-clean and all local sed is BSD-safe.

Signed-off-by: Jason Montleon <jmontleo@redhat.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
